STYLE: A magnificent hand-made toy theatre of printed cardboard, each piece a flat cutout of thick 4 mm card with visible raw brown cut edges. Painted in Chinese charcoal, soft graphite and luminous dry chalk pastel on textured blue-grey cotton rag paper, with coal-dust smudges and broad gentle strokes. Tender, recognizably Chinese faces, restrained human expressions, round brass split pins on articulated puppets. A fictional Chinese-speaking coal-mining town over several decades: worn blue cotton work jackets, simple homes, a pithead wheel, timbered mine entrance, a telescope, and later a planetarium. Palette: coal black #252B30, graphite #4E5962, paper slate #A3ADB4, chalk cream #ECE8DB, faded workwear blue #526C7B, warm ochre #B99159, lamp amber #DFB87C, deep star indigo #24334F, tiny chalk-silver stars #DCE6EA. Contrast the small amber domestic light with an immense indigo star canopy, ending in one warm light on two hands. Beautiful printed-card craft, quiet dignity, familial love and remembered labour.
CONSTRAINTS: No text, writing, lettering, numbers, labels, logos, signatures or watermarks. No national or company emblems. No photographic people, sculpted 3D characters, plastic, glossy finish or anime. No gore or graphic injury. Everything is flat painted card; actual rods, strings, sky, dust and light come from the theatre. A blind father remains alive, dignified, curious and loved. His sight is never magically restored.
Use case: illustration-story.
Image 1 is the selected key art, generated with gpt-image-2.6-sunburst. Preserve its exact charcoal-and-chalk material, palette and character identities. The older father in Image 1, grey hair, lined kind face, brown-grey work coat, blue collar, dark trousers, seated on the same simple wooden padded chair. A FOUR-PART seated marionette construction sheet, four fully separate shapes at a common drawing scale: (1) HEAD and neck alone, kindly listening expression and gently closed/unfocused eyes, three-quarter profile facing RIGHT, brass neck pin at the bottom; (2) his seated BODY WITH LAP, bent legs, shoes AND wooden chair as one connected card shape, NO head and NO arms, visible brass neck and two shoulder pins; (3) his full RIGHT-REACHING sleeved arm alone, shoulder brass pin to a large open UPWARD palm, roughly horizontal, the palm ready to receive the daughter’s tracing finger; (4) his other full sleeved arm, shoulder pin to relaxed hand for his lap. Keep the white cane tucked against the chair as part of the connected body/chair shape. Exactly four separate shapes and no extra loose cane. No labels or assembled duplicate. This is a living, proud father listening to his daughter, not a corpse. One isolated front-facing painted-card cutout on a genuinely transparent alpha background, with every gap transparent. No backdrop, sky, shadows, floor beyond the object, rods, strings, frame or lettering. Entire object inside the image with a generous clear margin. Raw brown card cut edge.
